\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 108; 2026-09-24), the asserted result is that complex exact and border determinant representations of the permanent require size of cubic order, with the stated branching-program consequences.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
Over $\mathbb C$, let $\operatorname{per}_m$ be the permanent of a generic $m\times m$ matrix. Its border determinantal complexity is the least $N$ for which it lies in the coefficientwise closure of determinants of $N\times N$ matrices with affine-linear entries. Exact determinantal complexity omits the closure. The asserted estimates are
\[
 \overline{\operatorname{dc}}(\operatorname{per}_m)\ge\frac{m^3}{5\,529\,600e},\qquad
 \operatorname{dc}(\operatorname{per}_m)\ge\frac{m^3}{5\,529\,600e}\quad(m\ge1408).
